  "response": "## The finding\n\n`crimes_00032` — **SVG With Embedded Raster**, severity `high`, confidence `0.95`, on `src/assets/partner-logo.svg`. Quoting the evidence verbatim:\n\n> - `2 <image href=\"data:image/…;base64,…\"> occurrences`\n> - `embedded MIME types: image/jpeg, image/png`\n> - `SVG byte size: 592 bytes (includes the base64 overhead)`\n> - `re-author the raster region as vector paths, or split it out to its own asset`\n\nSo: **2 embedded rasters**, MIME types **`image/jpeg` and `image/png`**, in a 592-byte file.\n\n## What's actually inside\n\nI decoded both payloads (`src/assets/partner-logo.svg:3-4`):\n\n| Region | MIME | Intrinsic size | Drawn at | base64 chars |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| left mark (`x=0`) | `image/png` | **1 × 1 px** | 80 × 80 | 92 |\n| right mark (`x=100`) | `image/jpeg` | **1 × 1 px** | 80 × 80 | 216 |\n\n308 of the file's 592 bytes — **52%** — is base64. And both rasters are single pixels stretched 80×, i.e. flat colour fills. There is no photographic detail in either one to preserve.\n\nTwo side observations worth folding into the same edit:\n- Line 4 uses `xlink:href` but the root `<svg>` never declares `xmlns:xlink`. That's an undeclared namespace prefix — strict XML parsers are entitled to reject it, and SVG 2 deprecated `xlink:href` in favour of plain `href` anyway.\n- Nothing in the fixture imports this file (`grep` for `partner-logo` across the repo returns nothing), so there are no call sites to update — the only reference to change is inside the SVG itself.\n\n## Remediation\n\n**Re-author as vector — both regions.** Given they're 1×1 stretched fills, each `<image>` maps to a single `<rect>` (or a `<path>` if the real partner marks have geometry the placeholder is standing in for). No standalone raster asset is warranted here; splitting a 1×1 pixel out to `partner-logo-mark.png` would trade base64 overhead for an extra HTTP request and still lock a flat colour to a resolution.\n\nConcrete steps:\n\n1. Get the true source geometry from the design tool (Figma/Illustrator). These 1×1 payloads are placeholders — the partner marks presumably exist as real vector artwork upstream. Export as SVG with *no* rasterisation.\n2. Replace both `<image>` elements with vector geometry in the same 200×80 viewBox, keeping the existing `x`/`y`/`width`/`height` layout boxes so the composition doesn't shift.\n3. Drop the `xlink:` prefix; use bare `href` if any external reference survives.\n4. Keep `<title>Partner logo</title>` and add `role=\"img\"` for assistive tech.\n5. Run `crimes scan --format json` again and confirm `svg_with_embedded_raster` no longer fires on this path.\n\nShape of the result — still `src/assets/partner-logo.svg`, no new files:\n\n```svg\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"200\" height=\"80\"\n     viewBox=\"0 0 200 80\" role=\"img\">\n  <title>Partner logo</title>\n  <!-- left mark: real partner-A path data from the design source -->\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#000\"/>\n  <!-- right mark: real partner-B path data from the design source -->\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"0\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n</svg>\n```\n\n**The fallback rule, if a real partner mark turns out to be photographic** (a gradient-heavy or textured logotype some brand guidelines mandate): don't inline it. Export it to `src/assets/partner-logo-<brand>.webp` alongside a `.png` fallback, keep the *vector* parts in the SVG, and compose the two in HTML with `<picture>` rather than nesting `<image href=\"./partner-logo-<brand>.webp\">` inside the SVG. Reason: a relative `href` inside an SVG resolves against the SVG's own URL when loaded via `<img src>`, but against the *host page* when the SVG is inlined into HTML — so an inlined SVG with a relative raster href silently 404s. `<picture>` sidesteps that entirely.\n\n## One caveat before anyone applies this\n\n`evals/fixtures/01-messy-ts-app/` is the intentional-mess fixture the detectors are tuned against, and per the repo's `CLAUDE.md` its finding set is calibration input. Fixing this SVG in place would stop `svg_with_embedded_raster` from firing and move the eval baseline — which per the versioning policy needs a patch bump plus a re-run of `pnpm run evals` in the same commit. I've deliberately not edited the file. Say the word if you want the fix applied to the fixture with that baseline update, or applied to a real (non-fixture) copy.",
